{"parentUuid":"e3d7f62b-0580-4494-bb8b-e2c5806fdb15","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bcf82525-84d7-4ef2-9e83-41c3e47b2780","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EPyH8PaMnFkNGiJWmVxFKE","type":"tool_result","content":"0\n      const owner = ownerOf(item);\n      if (item.object) cutFromGroup(item, Boolean(item.object.gone));\n      if (item.object && !owner && item.splats) item.splats.visible = false;\n      if (owner) {\n        placeShapes(item);\n        if (item.splats) {\n          shift.copy(offset).negate().applyQuaternion(spin);\n          item.splats.position.copy(owner.center).add(shift);\n          item.splats.quaternion.copy(spin);\n          // Class files hold this object too, so its own file only shows on its own when \n          const shared = Boolean(item.element.splat_group) && !state.isolated && !item.obj\n          item.splats.visible = real && item.mesh.visible && !shared;\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    for (const { mesh, cls } of splatGroups.values()) {\n      mesh.visible = real && !state.isolated && !state.hidden.has(cls);\n    }\n    // The section keeps what is below a height above the floor, like a plan cut.\n  // Taps and hovering use each element's simple shape in every look, even when it isn't drawn:\n  // scan meshes and splats have gaps, so a tap in the middle of a bucket could miss it.\n  // Equipment comes before walls and floor; among it, the front shape wins (see pick.js).\n  function candidate(raycaster) {\n    const shown = items.filter((item) => visible(item));\n    const inCut = (hit) => state.cut === null || section.distanceToPoint(hit.point) >= 0;\n    const front = (list) =>\n      pickFront(\n        raycaster,\n        list.map((item) => ({\n          mesh: item.box,\n          volume: item.volume,\n          thin: THIN_LABELS.has(item.element.psets.Valmet_Identification?.DetectedLabel),\n          surface: (rc) => surfaceAt(item, rc, inCut),\n          item,\n        })),\n        inCut,\n      )?.item ?? null;\n    const equipment = shown.filter((item) => !ROOM.has(item.element.ifc_class));\n    const room = shown.filter((item) => ROOM.has(item.element.ifc_class));\n    return front(equipment) ?? front(room);\n  }\n\n  // Distance to an element's real surface along a ray: its fitted shape, or its scan mesh.\n  function surfaceAt(item, raycaster, keep = () => true) {\n    const fitted = !item.box.userData.base.transparent;\n    const real = fitted ? item.box : item.scan;\n    if (!real) return null;\n    const hit = raycaster.intersectObject(real, false).find(keep);\n    return hit ? hit.distance : null;\n  }\n\n  // The same, for the scan view, where shapes are only placed when needed.\n73:      mesh.userData.home = mesh.position.clone();\n74:      mesh.userData.turn = mesh.quaternion.clone();\n364:  const offset = new THREE.Vector3();\n365:  const spin = new THREE.Quaternion();\n366:  const shift = new THREE.Vector3();\n374:      shift.copy(mesh.userData.home).sub(offset).applyQuaternion(spin);\n376:      mesh.quaternion.copy(mesh.userData.turn).premultiply(spin);\n=== checklist\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:4:unticked and add a line under **Bugs** at the end. Start with an empty scene: press **Undo chan\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:6:**Run it:** `./start browser`, then open http://localhost:8000/?tablet=0\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:17:- [ ] `make model` downloads the language model\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:22:- [ ] `./start browser` starts everything, and prints the address\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:23:- [ ] `./start tablet` starts everything, and prints the tablet's address\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:25:- [ ] `./start` says what's missing if a file is gone\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:26:- [ ] `./start` says so if the ports are already in use\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:27:- [ ] http://localhost:8001/api/health shows database, copilot and floor map as true\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:37:- [ ] **Range** changes how far frames and labels show: 2, 3, 5, 10 m\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:38:- [ ] **Boxes on/off** shows and hides frames\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:39:- [ ] **Scan**, **Both** and **Objects** views each look right\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:40:- [ ] **Apart** pulls objects apart, and **Together** brings them back\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:69:- [ ] **Move on floor** only shows on movable objects\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:86:- [ ] **Rotate on floor** only shows on movable objects\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:98:- [ ] **Add object** lets you draw a box around something\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:110:- [ ] **Undo changes** puts every moved and rotated object back\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:141:## 12. Copilot\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:142:- [ ] **Copilot** and **Ask copilot** open the window\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:162:- [ ] Speaking to the copilot (not built yet)\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:168:- [ ] Each action works: boxes, range, view, apart, BIM, reset, copilot\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:175:**Run it:** `./start tablet`, then open the address it prints, on the tablet.\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:185:- [ ] **Phone** mode works with HTTPS: turn to look, step to walk\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:186:- [ ] **Track** follows the device with ARCore (check scale by walking a known distance)\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:187:- [ ] Copilot answers and speaks on the tablet\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:194:- [ ] **Internet off:** scene, routes, moves, copilot and voice all work\ndocs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md:209:- [ ] Reach `P-005`: the copilot explains it, with sources and safe checks\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:12:  D --> E[\"5. Use it<br/>viewer, routes, copilot\"]\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:50:  M --> O[\"Build 3D objects and boxes<br/>app.extract.lift\"]\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:71:| Everything together | `make nav-check` | Floor, routes, links, copilot and moves work on real \ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:82:  API --> CP[\"Copilot<br/>app/copilot\"]\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:90:Start it with `./start browser` or `./start tablet`. The model runs on the server, never the tab\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:108:The original scan i