{"parentUuid":"14f01b58-8f81-4686-a30d-0ee5284e5581","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgovy7mYNgosDKvRC1wSP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**It's running: open http://localhost:8080** (the real scene and Val with Gemma). I loaded it once on this ThinkPad's own GPU: the room renders properly with the four main buttons and no page errors. I haven't clicked through this exact session, so tell me if anything looks off.\n\nOther devices on your network can use http://10.20.0.133:8080, if your firewall allows it.\n\n**Good things to try first:**\n- **Ask Val:** \"What needs attention?\", then \"Take me there\".\n- **Plan:** the bird's-eye view, where you can search for `P-005` or `tank`.\n- **Combine and BIM:** combine the black chair with its second box, then press **BIM** in **More** and switch looks.\n- **Duplicate or Delete:** tap any object, and press Esc to go back.\n\n**How this run differs from a normal start:**\n- **Port 8080, not 8000:** another project, \"CoolWatch\", is using 8000. I left it alone.\n- **Not started with `./start laptop`:** that needs the full `make` setup, which isn't on this machine, and it would trigger a large GPU package download. It would also refuse to start while 8000 is taken. It still hasn't been run anywhere, so your teammates will be the first to try it.\n- **Scratch data:** it runs the latest main (`085d410`), which includes a newer merge from Eduard's branch (#35), but the scene files are in my temp folder. The BIM files were built before the last few merges.\n- **No database:** moves, copies and deletes are lost if the API restarts.\n\n**To stop it:** `fuser -k 8080/tcp 8001/tcp`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2680,"cache_read_input_tokens":715036,"output_tokens":778,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":245},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_