{"parentUuid":"73aa8fb2-ca72-48f2-8c11-b8e2acb7278c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoyAAtraDcGW3J14DoxF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":492,"cache_read_input_tokens":749728,"output_tokens":2574,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1220},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":492,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2574,"cache_read_input_tokens":749728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":492,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":492},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":20705,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"fcb9b51f-05db-4b84-ad81-99a4aebfd426","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgoyAAZkr6KPec3u1DM5G","requestRef":"335aa3e1-8133-497e-8f2a-04634aff6324","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd12b257-f696-464c-84ba-f84686874f0e","timestamp":"2026-11-07T17:34:00.506Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/merge-team","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"dd12b257-f696-464c-84ba-f84686874f0e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoyAAtraDcGW3J14DoxF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**The site is closed:** ports 8080 and 8001 no longer respond. I've asked Ollama to unload Gemma too, though it still showed as loaded right after.\n\n**Going over your items:** you have **24 checklist lines**, not the 19 I said earlier, plus 3 bugs and 3 tasks in `docs/PLAN.md`. I didn't tick or change anything, since the checklist says only a person ticks.\n\n## A new bug on your list\n**Refused moves fail silently.** The collision message gets overwritten by \"N object(s) moved\", so the operator never learns why. A refused turn also still counts as a change, and the count goes up with every change rather than every object: it reached 9 in a session with four objects moved.\n\nThis matters for the demo because **the cart can't turn at either spot I checked**: it hits a bucket at its home spot and at the spot it moved to. Use the chair for the rotate demo; it turned fine.\n\n## Your lines\n| Status | Items |\n|---|---|\n| **Worked on the real scene, ready for you to tick** | Move, Rotate (drag and 45° buttons), Done, Collision warning, Plan search, Plan tap, Show pipes |\n| **Worked earlier, not rerun today** | Duplicate, Delete, Name it, Split, Combine |\n| **Needs your eyes** | Clean move of the three objects, Other objects, Floor under moved objects. My screenshots were too high up and blurry to judge |\n| **Needs hardware I don't have** | Two-finger twist (touch screen), DXF in a real CAD tool, Plan's scale (measure the room: the scan says 9.12 × 7.27 m) |\n| **Partly checked** | `make scene`: the 125 MB file is on the Release, but I didn't download it. `make pieces`, `highlights`, `bim`: the commands look right and the underlying steps ran earlier, but not through `make`, which would pull the large GPU packages |\n| **5090 only** | `make pipeline` for real, which also needs a SAM setup because Roihu is closed |\n| **Not run** | Video to splat is a manual process and I didn't run it today |\n| **Pitch only** | Update by short clip or rescan |\n| **Your call** | Duplicate: Valmet didn't ask for it. Add object suggestions: I haven't tested them with Gemma. Old spot unblocks: listed under you in one place and Eduard in another |\n\n## Your three bugs\n- **Undo route check:** it passed in both reruns on the latest main, 66 of 66, and 4.307 m both times. It failed once in all my runs, which fits test timing but doesn't prove it. I'd keep it as low priority.\n- **Load time:** this line is out of date. In three fresh loads each, the light scene takes about 6.5 s against about 10.5 s for the old full scene, on this machine with no backend running. The full scene itself is no faster, and `./start browser` still uses it.\n- **Delete takes neighbours:** still open. It may be fixable properly, because `splat_labels.npy` says which splats belong to each object, so it could hide just those instead of the whole box.\n\n## Your `docs/PLAN.md` tasks\n- **5090 rehearsal:** not done, and nothing has been tested on the 5090 yet.\n- **Ask Valmet which pump is P-005:** needs you.\n- **Confirm the deadline:** the checklist now says **tomorrow, Sunday 10:00**, while `docs/PLAN.md` still lists it as unconfirmed.\n\n## Checklist corrections\n- **Tablet line (Benjamin's):** it says \"tap a window to close it, no X\", but #32 brought the X back.\n- **Port 8000:** on this ThinkPad, `./start` will refuse to run while CoolWatch holds that port.\n\n## What I'd do next\n1. Fix the silent refusal and the wrong count, which is small and shows up in the demo.\n2. Make Delete hide only the object's own splats.\n\n**Do you want me to start on those two?** The 5090 rehearsal and the Valmet question are the most urgent things only you can do."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":492,"cache_read_input_tokens":749728,"output_tokens":2574,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1220},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":492,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2574,"cache_read_input_tokens":749728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":492,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":492},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"fcb9b51f-05db-4b84-ad81-99a4aebfd426","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgoyAAZkr6KPec3u1DM5G","requestRef":"335aa3e1-8133-497e-8f2a-04634aff6324","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"085debd9-b717-4289-8032-6d431f692902","timestamp":"2026-11-07T17:34:06.365Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/merge-team","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
