{"parentUuid":"7f87ecaa-6b9c-4258-a5c4-4ece314ce0b3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"24072eb3-f722-40d0-aa26-321dae0a2f81","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"image","source":{"type":"base64","media_type":"image/png","data":""}},{"type":"text","text":"First merge pull Benjamins  bugfixes. Start on those two then lets tackle the floor and wall being clickable in all the modes since they shouldn't be interactable, when isolating an object in BIM there is a bug where other object labels show up without reason (ss attached). CVal instructions still seem weird so keep stress testing it with different prompts an we make Val more human like/less chatbot style? We should also have colored bounding boxes depending on the groups (you can use the filtering that BIM views use) and you can decide the colors (so lets say pipes are 1 color, pumps are color 2 etc etc.) How are we handling new objects adding - do we need to shoot a video and resplat that specific area/ add the splats in there? If so how are we handling that? Regarding voice mode how heavy would be whisper/another TTS- STT model on top of our current deployment? How are we handling demo deployment - the deliverables allows us to submit a demo site (probably github.io, but that means we would need to use one computer as the server and if multiple people would check the demo it would explode?) what do you suggest?"}]},"uuid":"88d6477e-f322-4b42-9422-942b92161f95","timestamp":"2026-11-07T17:43:03.863Z","imagePasteIds":[3],"permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"sdk","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":150,"turnIndex":195},"turnAttributionKey":"REDACTED","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/merge-team","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
