{"parentUuid":"0811a627-45b8-4d6f-b86a-261d690ac018","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"24072eb3-f722-40d0-aa26-321dae0a2f81","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019NfJBNH3Xu1cbpL8sPM5P2","type":"tool_result","content":"57e6132 Benjamin Sundell Update Benjamin's handoff for the fix list\na9582b2 Benjamin Sundell Plan: a light 2D blueprint instead of the heavy floor layout\nc98df64 Benjamin Sundell Tests: copies block routes, and routes stay inside the floor map\n111ce6b Benjamin Sundell Viewer: start just inside the door, facing into the room\n04d476b Benjamin Sundell Walk keeps to the walkable floor; Fly stays free\n7c33215 Benjamin Sundell Viewer: raise and lower objects and their copies (Page Up/Down)\nfcde959 Benjamin Sundell Remove info only: drop a junk detection's box and data, keep it in the scan\nc833536 Benjamin Sundell Viewer: keyboard shortcuts (Delete, Ctrl+Z, M, R, C, N, F, G)\n414666d Benjamin Sundell Undo the latest change, next to Reset all\n35f63cb Benjamin Sundell Viewer: Rotate lives under Move, and hide the View button BIM replaces\ne21c444 Benjamin Sundell Viewer: stop the flicker while moving, and keep typing out of the camera\n77e1e54 Eduard Rednic Split the checklist across the five team members\n32d6def Eduard Rednic Correct the checklist's line on viewer commands\n441f617 Eduard Rednic Remake the checklist with status, decisions and every deliverable\n app/api/main.py              |  46 +++-\n app/api/store.py             |  27 +++\n docs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md       | 500 ++++++++++++++++++++++------------\n handoffs/benjamin-sundell.md |  12 +-\n handoffs/eduard-rednic.md    |   8 +-\n tests/test_api.py            | 108 ++++++++++\n web/bim.js                   |   3 +-\n web/index.html               |  13 +-\n web/main.js                  | 173 +++++++++++++--\n web/objects.js               |  21 +-\n web/plan.js                  | 287 ++++++++++++++++---------\n web/style.css                |   4 +-\n web/walkable.js              |  73 +++++++\n 13 files changed, 899 insertions(+), 376 deletions(-)\n=== eduard's val results\nRecord Val test results and swap test parts with Hannu\n\n docs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md    | 47 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------\n handoffs/eduard-rednic.md | 10 +++++-----\n 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)\n+| **Eduard** | Val. Scoring: navigation, backend. Setup: database, nav-check, `./start` |\n-| **Hannu** | Val. Scoring: AI diagnostics. Setup: mapping, language models |\n-- [ ] **How Val knows:** evidence, causes, confidence. ✅ 🤖 KEEP\n-- [ ] **Safety refusal:** Hannu's rule. Misses \"Shut down\", \"Close CV-003\", \"Isolate\". 🟡 🤖 Hannu to DECIDE\n-- [ ] **Safety refusal, false alarms:** refuses \"What does drain mean?\". 🟡 🤖 Hannu to DECIDE\n+- [x] **How Val knows:** evidence, causes, confidence. ✅ 🤖 KEEP\n+- [ ] **Safety refusal:** not working. Misses \"Shut down\", \"Close CV-003\", \"Isolate\". It must reply \"I can't do that\". 🟡 🤖 Hannu to DECIDE\n+- [ ] **Safety refusal, false alarms:** not working. \"What does drain mean?\" gets refused and repeats the previous message. Val must give its own reply. 🟡 🤖 Hannu to DECIDE\n+- [ ] **Unclear or off-topic messages:** for vague or unrelated messages, Val says it doesn't understand. ❌ ❌ ADD\n+- [ ] **Typing in Val's chat:** W, A, S and D move the view while typing. Keys must only go to the chat while it's in use. ❌ 👤 ADD\n-- [ ] **Speaking to Val:** ❌ ❌ DECIDE. Needs offline speech-to-text. First to cut\n-- [ ] **Val doing actions by voice:** commands exist, with nothing connecting speech. 🟡 ❌ DECIDE\n+- [ ] **Answers read aloud:** we don't need Val to talk. ✅ 👤 CUT\n+- [ ] **Speaking to Val:** to do. Needs offline speech-to-text. ❌ ❌ ADD. First to cut\n+- [ ] **Val doing actions:** to do. Link every button to phrases that trigger it. The target comes from the device named in the sentence, or from what's selected. If it's unclear, Val asks. Commands \n=== plan.js now\n431 web/plan.js\n// Plan: a 2D blueprint of the room from above, with the walls, the equipment, the route, and where\n// you are. Generated from the scan, not surveyed, and it says so on screen.\n//\n// It's light on purpose. Walls and the room outline come from the BIM model (bim.json, built\n// offline), the walkable floor from /api/plan/walkable, and equipment from the objects as they stan\n// now. Nothing heavy is computed to open it, and it redraws at most about ten times a second.\n\nconst PADDING = 16;\nconst LABEL_HEIGHT = 16;\nconst MARGIN_M = 0.5; // metres of paper around the room\nconst FRAME_MS = 100;\n\n=== bugs\n## Bugs\nWrite them like this: `- [ ] Section: what you did, what happened, who's fixing it`\n- [ ] Undo: a route check failed once, showing 4.69 m. Looks like test timing, not confirmed. Viktor\n- [ ] Delete: hides the object's whole box, including neighbours. Viktor\n- [ ] Move: a moved object's old spot can stay blocked. Eduard\n- [ ] Load time didn't improve. Viktor\n=== handoff ben\n# benjamin-sundell: benjamin/fixes\n**Goal:** the team's bug and fix list for the viewer, on top of main (PR #35)\n**Done:** flicker fixed (adaptive resolution resized the canvas; now opt-in `?adaptive=1`); typing in Val no longer moves the camera; Rotate is a mode of Move; View button hidden (BIM replaces it); Undo (latest change, new `POST /api/changes/undo`) next to Reset all, and the viewer brings back undone deletes; hotkeys (Delete, Ctrl+Z, M, R, PgUp/PgDn, C, N, F, G, Esc); \"Remove info\" keeps a junk ob\n**Verified:** `make check` passes (275 passed, 4 skipped). Not yet clicked through in a browser\n**Next:** click through every fix; push and PR; tell Eduard (store.py, main.py endpoints), Viktor (plan.js, pacing default), Sasha (bim.js). Val stress test skipped (no model here). Database dummy data and demo deployment: decisions for the team\n**Blockers:** none","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fc853470-2421-4abb-95d7-9f12b4b68264","timestamp":"2026-11-07T17:43:39.967Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"57e6132 Benjamin Sundell Update Benjamin's handoff for the fix list\na9582b2 Benjamin Sundell Plan: a light 2D blueprint instead of the heavy floor layout\nc98df64 Benjamin Sundell Tests: copies block routes, and routes stay inside the floor map\n111ce6b Benjamin Sundell Viewer: start just inside the door, facing into the room\n04d476b Benjamin Sundell Walk keeps to the walkable floor; Fly stays free\n7c33215 Benjamin Sundell Viewer: raise and lower objects and their copies (Page Up/Down)\nfcde959 Benjamin Sundell Remove info only: drop a junk detection's box and data, keep it in the scan\nc833536 Benjamin Sundell Viewer: keyboard shortcuts (Delete, Ctrl+Z, M, R, C, N, F, G)\n414666d Benjamin Sundell Undo the latest change, next to Reset all\n35f63cb Benjamin Sundell Viewer: Rotate lives under Move, and hide the View button BIM replaces\ne21c444 Benjamin Sundell Viewer: stop the flicker while moving, and keep typing out of the camera\n77e1e54 Eduard Rednic Split the checklist across the five team members\n32d6def Eduard Rednic Correct the checklist's line on viewer commands\n441f617 Eduard Rednic Remake the checklist with status, decisions and every deliverable\n app/api/main.py              |  46 +++-\n app/api/store.py             |  27 +++\n docs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md       | 500 ++++++++++++++++++++++------------\n handoffs/benjamin-sundell.md |  12 +-\n handoffs/eduard-rednic.md    |   8 +-\n tests/test_api.py            | 108 ++++++++++\n web/bim.js                   |   3 +-\n web/index.html               |  13 +-\n web/main.js                  | 173 +++++++++++++--\n web/objects.js               |  21 +-\n web/plan.js                  | 287 ++++++++++++++++---------\n web/style.css                |   4 +-\n web/walkable.js              |  73 +++++++\n 13 files changed, 899 insertions(+), 376 deletions(-)\n=== eduard's val results\nRecord Val test results and swap test parts with Hannu\n\n docs/TEST_CHECKLIST.md    | 47 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------\n handoffs/eduard-rednic.md | 10 +++++-----\n 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)\n+| **Eduard** | Val. Scoring: navigation, backend. Setup: database, nav-check, `./start` |\n-| **Hannu** | Val. Scoring: AI diagnostics. Setup: mapping, language models |\n-- [ ] **How Val knows:** evidence, causes, confidence. ✅ 🤖 KEEP\n-- [ ] **Safety refusal:** Hannu's rule. Misses \"Shut down\", \"Close CV-003\", \"Isolate\". 🟡 🤖 Hannu to DECIDE\n-- [ ] **Safety refusal, false alarms:** refuses \"What does drain mean?\". 🟡 🤖 Hannu to DECIDE\n+- [x] **How Val knows:** evidence, causes, confidence. ✅ 🤖 KEEP\n+- [ ] **Safety refusal:** not working. Misses \"Shut down\", \"Close CV-003\", \"Isolate\". It must reply \"I can't do that\". 🟡 🤖 Hannu to DECIDE\n+- [ ] **Safety refusal, false alarms:** not working. \"What does drain mean?\" gets refused and repeats the previous message. Val must give its own reply. 🟡 🤖 Hannu to DECIDE\n+- [ ] **Unclear or off-topic messages:** for vague or unrelated messages, Val says it doesn't understand. ❌ ❌ ADD\n+- [ ] **Typing in Val's chat:** W, A, S and D move the view while typing. Keys must only go to the chat while it's in use. ❌ 👤 ADD\n-- [ ] **Speaking to Val:** ❌ ❌ DECIDE. Needs offline speech-to-text. First to cut\n-- [ ] **Val doing actions by voice:** commands exist, with nothing connecting speech. 🟡 ❌ DECIDE\n+- [ ] **Answers read aloud:** we don't need Val to talk. ✅ 👤 CUT\n+- [ ] **Speaking to Val:** to do. Needs offline speech-to-text. ❌ ❌ ADD. First to cut\n+- [ ] **Val doing actions:** to do. Link every button to phrases that trigger it. The target comes from the device named in the sentence, or from what's selected. If it's unclear, Val asks. Commands \n=== plan.js now\n431 web/plan.js\n// Plan: a 2D blueprint of the room from above, with the walls, the equipment, the route, and where\n// you are. Generated from the scan, not surveyed, and it says so on screen.\n//\n// It's light on purpose. Walls and the room outline come from the BIM model (bim.json, built\n// offline), the walkable floor from /api/plan/walkable, and equipment from the objects as they stan\n// now. Nothing heavy is computed to open it, and it redraws at most about ten times a second.\n\nconst PADDING = 16;\nconst LABEL_HEIGHT = 16;\nconst MARGIN_M = 0.5; // metres of paper around the room\nconst FRAME_MS = 100;\n\n=== bugs\n## Bugs\nWrite them like this: `- [ ] Section: what you did, what happened, who's fixing it`\n- [ ] Undo: a route check failed once, showing 4.69 m. Looks like test timing, not confirmed. Viktor\n- [ ] Delete: hides the object's whole box, including neighbours. Viktor\n- [ ] Move: a moved object's old spot can stay blocked. Eduard\n- [ ] Load time didn't improve. Viktor\n=== handoff ben\n# benjamin-sundell: benjamin/fixes\n**Goal:** the team's bug and fix list for the viewer, on top of main (PR #35)\n**Done:** flicker fixed (adaptive resolution resized the canvas; now opt-in `?adaptive=1`); typing in Val no longer moves the camera; Rotate is a mode of Move; View button hidden (BIM replaces it); Undo (latest change, new `POST /api/changes/undo`) next to Reset all, and the viewer brings back undone deletes; hotkeys (Delete, Ctrl+Z, M, R, PgUp/PgDn, C, N, F, G, Esc); \"Remove info\" keeps a junk ob\n**Verified:** `make check` passes (275 passed, 4 skipped). Not yet clicked through in a browser\n**Next:** click through every fix; push and PR; tell Eduard (store.py, main.py endpoints), Viktor (plan.js, pacing default), Sasha (bim.js). Val stress test skipped (no model here). Database dummy data and demo deployment: decisions for the team\n**Blockers:** none","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"67a3ffae-df0b-4727-ac35-5a1b5dfc6585","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","root":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude