{"parentUuid":"67121353-22f4-4470-a3d8-cf626357b294","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"24072eb3-f722-40d0-aa26-321dae0a2f81","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014FRR6iBgqEmXh2sdQbpQM5","type":"tool_result","content":"THANKS_WORDS = (\n    r\"((ok|okay|great|cool|nice|perfect|got it|good)[ ,]*)?\"\n    r\"(thanks|thank you|thx|kiitos|ok|okay|great|cool|nice|perfect|got it)?( so much| a lot)?( val)?\"\n)\n    \"current\": (\"current_a\", \"Motor current\", \" A\"),\n}\nMEASUREMENT_WORDS = (\"measurement\", \"reading\", \"telemetry\", \"sensor\", \"getting worse\", \"getting better\",\n                     \"trend\", \"changed recently\")  # fmt: skip\n2 files reformatted, 89 files left uncha\nE501 Line too long (101 > 100)\n   --> app/copilot/copilot.py:100:101\nE501 Line too long (104 > 100)\n   --> app/copilot/copilot.py:123:101\nE501 Line too long (101 > 100)\n   --> app/copilot/tools.py:272:101\n[-] 'anything urgent?'\n   4 devices are marked high urgency. I'd start with P-005: its health is 44 out of 100, and the records point to efficiency loss / fouling-like signature. The first check is: inspect hydraulic path. After\n[-] \"what's wrong?\"\n   The plant's records don't cover that, so I won't guess. Try asking what needs attention, or tap a device and ask what's wrong with it.\n[-] 'is everything ok?'\n   4 devices are marked high urgency. I'd start with P-005: its health is 44 out of 100, and the records point to efficiency loss / fouling-like signature. The first check is: inspect hydraulic path. After\n[-] 'how many pumps are there?'\n   The records list 6 pumps: P-001, P-002, P-003, P-004, P-005, P-006.\n[-] 'what should I do first?'\n   4 devices are marked high urgency. I'd start with P-005: its health is 44 out of 100, and the records point to efficiency loss / fouling-like signature. The first check is: inspect hydraulic path. After\n[-] 'tell me about P-005'\n   This is P-005, a process pump in Utility Island. Right now it needs attention, with its health at 44 out of 100.\n[-] 'take me to the faulty pump'\n   I've marked P-005 and drawn the route to it. Its link to this object is only 30% certain, so check the nameplate when you get there.\n[-] 'take me to the kitchen'\n   I don't know where the kitchen is. I can only take you to equipment in this room, so tap a device or give me a tag like P-005.\n[-] 'when was CV-001 last serviced?'\n[obj-0049] 'how do I fix it?'\n   For P-005, I'd start with this check: inspect hydraulic path. The guidance also says to look at several readings together and confirm it on site. Get the proper permits and follow lockout/tagout before \n[obj-0049] 'is it dangerous?'\n   I can't tell you that it's safe. Only the site's procedures and qualified staff can. What I can say is that P-005 needs attention. Get a permit and follow lockout/tagout before any work.\n[obj-0049] 'is it safe to work on?'\n   I can't tell you that it's safe. Only the site's procedures and qualified staff can. What I can say is that P-005 needs attention. Get a permit and follow lockout/tagout before any work.\n[obj-0049] 'how urgent is this?'\n   P-005 is marked high urgency, with its health at 44 out of 100. Its criticality is listed as A - production critical.\n[obj-0049] 'what is this?'\n   This is P-005, a process pump in Utility Island. Right now it needs attention, with its health at 44 out of 100.\n[obj-0049] 'what parts do I need?'\n   I don't have records on spare parts, so I won't guess. I can see each device's condition, measurements, events, work orders and guidance documents.\n[obj-0049] 'who do I call?'\n   I don't have records on contacts, so I won't guess. I can see each device's condition, measurements, events, work orders and guidance documents.\n[obj-0049] 'what is the manual for this?'\n   I don't have a manual, but this guidance covers P-005: Process pump condition context (DOC-PROCESS_PUMP-CORE); Field-service safety guardrail (DOC-FIELD-SAFETY); Evidence-grounded AI response contract (\n[obj-0049] 'explain the health score'\n   P-005 needs attention. Its health is 44 out of 100, and the records point to efficiency loss / fouling-like signature. I'd start with this check: inspect hydraulic path. Follow the site's safety rules b\n[obj-0049] 'tell me more'\n   P-005 needs attention. Its health is 44 out of 100, and the records point to efficiency loss / fouling-like signature. I'd start with this check: inspect hydraulic path. Follow the site's safety rules b\n[obj-0067] 'what is this?'\n   The scan shows this as: cart. It isn't linked to a plant record, so I have no condition, measurements or service history for it, and I won't guess which device it is. I can take you to it so you can che\n[obj-0067] 'is it movable?'\n   Yes, it's marked as movable. Press Move in its panel.\n[obj-0049] 'shut it down'\n   REFUSED I can't do that. I don't operate equipment, I only read the records and explain them. If it needs doing, follow lockout/tagout and the site's permits, and have qualified staff do it.\n[obj-0049] 'can I restart it?'\n   REFUSED I can't do that. I don't operate equipment, I only read the records and explain them. If it needs doing, follow lockout/tagout and the site's permits, and have qualified staff do it.\n[obj-0049] 'should I shut it down?'\n   REFUSED I can't do that. I don't operate equipment, I only read the records and explain them. If it needs doing, follow lockout/tagout and the site's permits, and have qualified staff do it.\n[-] 'What does drain mean?'\n   The plant's records don't cover that, so I won't guess. Try asking what needs attention, or tap a device and ask what's wrong with it.\n[-] 'what does shut down mean'\n   The plant's records don't cover that, so I won't guess. Try asking what needs attention, or tap a device and ask what's wrong with it.\n[-] 'what is fouling?'\n   The plant's records don't cover that, so I won't guess. Try asking what needs attention, or tap a device and ask what's wrong with it.\n[-] 'why did the valve close?'\n   Which valve do you mean? Tap it, or give me its tag.\n[-] 'is the valve open?'\n   Which valve do you mean? Tap it, or give me its tag.\n.......................................................s..........s..... [ 98%]\n....                                                                     [100%]\n=============================== warnings summary ===============================\n../../.cache/uv/archive-v0/GiLBwBEKwRTxYXseTw-TM/lib/python3.12/site-packages/fastapi/testclient.py:1\n  /home/viktor-trilar/.cache/uv/archive-v0/GiLBwBEKwRTxYXseTw-TM/lib/python3.12/site-packages/fastapi/testclient.py:1: StarletteDeprecationWarning: Us\n    from starlette.testclient import TestClient as TestClient  # noqa\n\n-- Docs: https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/capture-warnings.html\n290 passed, 3 skipped, 1 warning in 76.39s (0:01:16)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"adc23518-3e15-489a-b353-2ca602f9ea3b","timestamp":"2026-11-07T18:02:31.265Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"THANKS_WORDS = (\n    r\"((ok|okay|great|cool|nice|perfect|got it|good)[ ,]*)?\"\n    r\"(thanks|thank you|thx|kiitos|ok|okay|great|cool|nice|perfect|got it)?( so much| a lot)?( val)?\"\n)\n    \"current\": (\"current_a\", \"Motor current\", \" A\"),\n}\nMEASUREMENT_WORDS = (\"measurement\", \"reading\", \"telemetry\", \"sensor\", \"getting worse\", \"getting better\",\n                     \"trend\", \"changed recently\")  # fmt: skip\n2 files reformatted, 89 files left uncha\nE501 Line too long (101 > 100)\n   --> app/copilot/copilot.py:100:101\nE501 Line too long (104 > 100)\n   --> app/copilot/copilot.py:123:101\nE501 Line too long (101 > 100)\n   --> app/copilot/tools.py:272:101\n[-] 'anything urgent?'\n   4 devices are marked high urgency. I'd start with P-005: its health is 44 out of 100, and the records point to efficiency loss / fouling-like signature. The first check is: inspect hydraulic path. After\n[-] \"what's wrong?\"\n   The plant's records don't c