{"parentUuid":"a2d53b71-4ff1-456a-a937-e030f873a34c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgp2kSFd2czaWs6ALjnBs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AnEsYdKyTTfEbencwwPXWr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa; R=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; cd \"$W\"; python3 - <<'EOF'\nt = open(\"docs/RESULTS.md\").read()\nmarker = \"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Viewer frame rate on the demo laptop\"\nassert marker in t\nrows = (\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Viewer frame rate after Benjamin's fixes | Real GPU through Vulkan, 1280 x 800, light scene with pre-cut objects | Default, and with `?adaptive=1` | Turning: 16 frames a second by default, 32 with adaptive. Still: 59. Moving the mouse: 50, was 19 before a hover change drew one frame | | | ThinkPad, Ryzen 7 PRO 4750U, integrated graphics |\\n\"\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Load time, three fresh browsers each | No backend, on the same machine | Light scene against the full scene | Light 93 MB: 7.6, 6.5, 6.4 s. Full 396 MB: 11.1, 9.9, 10.0 s now, 11.1, 10.4, 10.5 s before this work | | | ThinkPad |\\n\"\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Delete hides the object's own splats | All 440 objects, `splat_labels.npy` | Up to 12 small boxes per object, inside its own box | Median 6 boxes. Other splats hidden: 636,785 against 801,748 for whole boxes, 21% fewer. Own splats still hidden: 99.8% | | | ThinkPad |\\n\"\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Speech to text for a voice mode | One 11 s English sample, faster-whisper, int8, 8 threads | tiny.en, base.en, small.en | tiny.en 75 MB: 0.6 s, 0.28 GB RAM. base.en 141 MB: 0.9 s, 0.35 GB. small.en 464 MB: 2.2 s, 0.64 GB. One clean sample, so no accuracy figure | | | ThinkPad, CPU only |\\n\"\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Val stress test | About 90 prompts, records answers only, read by eye | Greetings, off-topic, device questions, control requests, injection | Found and fixed: \\\"Shut it down\\\" and \\\"Can I restart it?\\\" not refused, \\\"Take me to the kitchen\\\" routing to the last device, \\\"Is the valve open?\\\" answering about a pump. Not scored, and the model's wording wasn't retested | | | ThinkPad |\\n\"\n)\nopen(\"docs/RESULTS.md\", \"w\").write(t.replace(marker, rows + marker, 1))\nopen(\"handoffs/viktortrilar.md\", \"w\").write(\"\"\"# viktortrilar: viktor/polish\n**Goal:** the next fix list: refused moves, Delete, floor and walls, BIM isolate labels, frame colours, and a more human Val\n**Done:** a refused move or turn says why and records nothing (web/objects.js). Delete hides small boxes around the object's own splats (app/scene/cover.py, `/api/objects/{id}/cover`). Walls and floor can't be picked or hovered. Isolate shows only that object's label. Frames coloured by type (web/colors.js), with a legend in More. Val talks like a person, gives specific answers, asks which device when unclear, and refuses more control requests. Voice starts off\n**Verified:** 290+ tests with the Excel pack, lint clean. Real GPU: 12 of 12 viewer checks, 28 of 28 combine and delete checks. 66 of 66 route checks. About 90 Val prompts read by eye. Not tested: Gemma's plain words on the new answers, tablet, 5090\n**Next:** merge this. Rehearse on the 5090. Decide on adaptive resolution: 16 frames a second turning by default, 32 with `?adaptive=1`, which Benjamin turned off for flicker\n**Blockers:** Valmet still has to confirm which pump is P-005. Objects made in the viewer still delete by whole box. Val only knows the phrases it's been given. Roihu closed until at least Monday\n\"\"\")\nEOF\nuv run --only-group dev ruff format . 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-40; make lint 2>&1 | grep -E \"^[A-Z][0-9]+ |All checks\" | cut -c1-70; (cd \"$R\" && PYTHONPATH=\"$W\" uv run --no-project --with numpy --with scipy --with pandas --with openpyxl --with pytest --with fastapi --with httpx --with pillow --with 'psycopg[binary]' --with ifcopenshell --with ezdxf pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider \"$W/tests\" --rootdir=\"$W\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-90); git add -A app docs handoffs scripts tests web; git status --short | grep -v \"^[AMDR] \" | cut -c1-50; git commit -q -m \"Make Val talk like a person, and fix refused moves, Delete and BIM picks\n\nVal: specific answers, plain refusals, it asks which device when unclear, and\nit refuses more control requests. A stress test found \\\"Shut it down\\\" wasn't\nrefused and \\\"Take me to the kitchen\\\" routed to the last device.\nViewer: a refused move says why and records nothing. Delete hides the object's\nown splats, not its whole box. Walls and floor can't be picked. Isolate hides\nother labels. Frames are coloured by type, the same as BIM mode.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"; git log --oneline -1 | cut -c1-70; git fetch -q origin; echo \"main moved: $(git rev-list --count HEAD..origin/main)\"; git log --format='%h %an %s' HEAD..origin/main | head -5 | cut -c1-90; git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only origin/main HEAD 2>&1 | sed -n '2,/^$/p' | grep -v '^$' | head -6 | cut -c1-50; git push -q git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git viktor/polish 2>&1 | grep -v \"^remote:\" | tail -1 | cut -c1-80; cat > \"$S/pr8.md\" <<'EOF'\nThe next fix list, on top of Benjamin's fixes. Also includes Eduard's Val test notes.\n\n**Val:**\n- Replies read like a colleague talking, not a database report. Tags and sources stay in the Sources line.\n- Specific questions get specific answers: measurements, urgency, past cases, confidence, documents.\n- If a reading doesn't exist, it says so. P-005 has no vibration readings, and Val now says that and gives what is measured.\n- It asks \"Which valve do you mean?\" when it's unclear, and says it's not sure when a message makes no sense.\n- It never says equipment is safe to work on.\n- Voice starts off.\n\n**Stress test, about 90 prompts read by eye. Found and fixed:**\n- \"Shut it down\", \"Can I restart it?\", \"Should I shut it down?\", \"Close CV-003\" and \"Isolate the pump\" weren't refused.\n- \"What does drain mean?\" was refused.\n- \"Take me to the kitchen\" routed to the last device.\n- \"Is the valve open?\" and \"What is the manual for this?\" answered about the last device.\n\n**Viewer:**\n- A refused move or turn says why, and records nothing. The old count of \"N objects moved\" is gone.\n- Delete hides up to 12 small boxes around the object's own splats, using `splat_labels.npy`. Across 440 objects that hides 21% fewer other splats than whole boxes, and still 99.8% of its own. Objects made in the viewer still use their whole box.\n- Walls and floor can't be picked or hovered in any BIM look.\n- Isolating in BIM shows only that object's label. Hidden types lose their labels too.\n- Frames are coloured by type, using BIM's groups, with a legend under More. The faulty device stays red.\n\n**Tested:**\n- 290+ tests with the Excel pack, lint clean.\n- On the ThinkPad's real GPU: 12 of 12 viewer checks, and 28 of 28 combine, delete, duplicate and back checks.\n- 66 of 66 route checks.\n\n**Not tested:** Gemma's \"In plain words\" on the new answers, a tablet, the 5090. The Val test was read by eye, not scored.\n\n**Decision needed:** Benjamin turned adaptive resolution off because of flicker. Turning is 16 frames a second by default, and 32 with `?adaptive=1`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\ngh pr create --base main --head viktor/polish --title \"Make Val talk like a person, and fix refused moves, Delete and BIM picks\" --body-file \"$S/pr8.md\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-80; sleep 8; timeout 100 gh pr checks viktor/polish --watch --interval 8 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-60; gh pr view viktor/polish --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus,number --jq '\"#\\(.number) \\(.mergeable) \\(.mergeStateStatus)\"'","description":"Run final checks, commit, push and open the pull request","timeout":280000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2760,"cache_read_input_tokens":846152,"output_tokens":3484,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":95},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2760,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3484,"cache_read_input_tokens":846152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2760,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2760},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":27801,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01AnEsYdKyTTfEbencwwPXWr":{"command":"W=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa; R=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; cd \"$W\"; python3 - <<'EOF'\nt = open(\"docs/RESULTS.md\").read()\nmarker = \"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Viewer frame rate on the demo laptop\"\nassert marker in t\nrows = (\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Viewer frame rate after Benjamin's fixes | Real GPU through Vulkan, 1280 x 800, light scene with pre-cut objects | Default, and with `?adaptive=1` | Turning: 16 frames a second by default, 32 with adaptive. Still: 59. Moving the mouse: 50, was 19 before a hover change drew one frame | | | ThinkPad, Ryzen 7 PRO 4750U, integrated graphics |\\n\"\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Load time, three fresh browsers each | No backend, on the same machine | Light scene against the full scene | Light 93 MB: 7.6, 6.5, 6.4 s. Full 396 MB: 11.1, 9.9, 10.0 s now, 11.1, 10.4, 10.5 s before this work | | | ThinkPad |\\n\"\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Delete hides the object's own splats | All 440 objects, `splat_labels.npy` | Up to 12 small boxes per object, inside its own box | Median 6 boxes. Other splats hidden: 636,785 against 801,748 for whole boxes, 21% fewer. Own splats still hidden: 99.8% | | | ThinkPad |\\n\"\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Speech to text for a voice mode | One 11 s English sample, faster-whisper, int8, 8 threads | tiny.en, base.en, small.en | tiny.en 75 MB: 0.6 s, 0.28 GB RAM. base.en 141 MB: 0.9 s, 0.35 GB. small.en 464 MB: 2.2 s, 0.64 GB. One clean sample, so no accuracy figure | | | ThinkPad, CPU only |\\n\"\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Val stress test | About 90 prompts, records answers only, read by eye | Greetings, off-topic, device questions, control requests, injection | Found and fixed: \\\"Shut it down\\\" and \\\"Can I restart it?\\\" not refused, \\\"Take me to the kitchen\\\" routing to the last device, \\\"Is the valve open?\\\" answering about a pump. Not scored, and the model's wording wasn't retested | | | ThinkPad |\\n\"\n)\nopen(\"docs/RESULTS.md\", \"w\").write(t.replace(marker, rows + marker, 1))\nopen(\"handoffs/viktortrilar.md\", \"w\").write(\"\"\"# viktortrilar: viktor/polish\n**Goal:** the next fix list: refused moves, Delete, floor and walls, BIM isolate labels, frame colours, and a more human Val\n**Done:** a refused move or turn says why and records nothing (web/objects.js). Delete hides small boxes around the object's own splats (app/scene/cover.py, `/api/objects/{id}/cover`). Walls and floor can't be picked or hovered. Isolate shows only that object's label. Frames coloured by type (web/colors.js), with a legend in More. Val talks like a person, gives specific answers, asks which device when unclear, and refuses more control requests. Voice starts off\n**Verified:** 290+ tests with the Excel pack, lint clean. Real GPU: 12 of 12 viewer checks, 28 of 28 combine and delete checks. 66 of 66 route checks. About 90 Val prompts read by eye. Not tested: Gemma's plain words on the new answers, tablet, 5090\n**Next:** merge this. Rehearse on the 5090. Decide on adaptive resolution: 16 frames a second turning by default, 32 with `?adaptive=1`, which Benjamin turned off for flicker\n**Blockers:** Valmet still has to confirm which pump is P-005. Objects made in the viewer still delete by whole box. Val only knows the phrases it's been given. Roihu closed until at least Monday\n\"\"\")\nEOF\nuv run --only-group dev ruff format . 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-40; make lint 2>&1 | grep -E \"^[A-Z][0-9]+ |All checks\" | cut -c1-70; (cd \"$R\" && PYTHONPATH=\"$W\" uv run --no-project --with numpy --with scipy --with pandas --with openpyxl --with pytest --with fastapi --with httpx --with pillow --with 'psycopg[binary]' --with ifcopenshell --with ezdxf pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider \"$W/tests\" --rootdir=\"$W\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-90); git add -A app docs handoffs scripts tests web; git status --short | grep -v \"^[AMDR] \" | cut -c1-50; git commit -q -m \"Make Val talk like a person, and fix refused moves, Delete and BIM picks\n\nVal: specific answers, plain refusals, it asks which device when unclear, and\nit refuses more control requests. A stress test found \\\"Shut it down\\\" wasn't\nrefused and \\\"Take me to the kitchen\\\" routed to the last device.\nViewer: a refused move says why and records nothing. Delete hides the object's\nown splats, not its whole box. Walls and floor can't be picked. Isolate hides\nother labels. Frames are coloured by type, the same as BIM mode.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"; git log --oneline -1 | cut -c1-70; git fetch -q origin; echo \"main moved: $(git rev-list --count HEAD..origin/main)\"; git log --format='%h %an %s' HEAD..origin/main | head -5 | cut -c1-90; git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only origin/main HEAD 2>&1 | sed -n '2,/^$/p' | grep -v '^$' | head -6 | cut -c1-50; git push -q git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git viktor/polish 2>&1 | grep -v \"^remote:\" | tail -1 | cut -c1-80; cat > \"$S/pr8.md\" <<'EOF'\nThe next fix list, on top of Benjamin's fixes. Also includes Eduard's Val test notes.\n\n**Val:**\n- Replies read like a colleague talking, not a database report. Tags and sources stay in the Sources line.\n- Specific questions get specific answers: measurements, urgency, past cases, confidence, documents.\n- If a reading doesn't exist, it says so. P-005 has no vibration readings, and Val now says that and gives what is measured.\n- It asks \"Which valve do you mean?\" when it's unclear, and says it's not sure when a message makes no sense.\n- It never says equipment is safe to work on.\n- Voice starts off.\n\n**Stress test, about 90 prompts read by eye. Found and fixed:**\n- \"Shut it down\", \"Can I restart it?\", \"Should I shut it down?\", \"Close CV-003\" and \"Isolate the pump\" weren't refused.\n- \"What does drain mean?\" was refused.\n- \"Take me to the kitchen\" routed to the last device.\n- \"Is the valve open?\" and \"What is the manual for this?\" answered about the last device.\n\n**Viewer:**\n- A refused move or turn says why, and records nothing. The old count of \"N objects moved\" is gone.\n- Delete hides up to 12 small boxes around the object's own splats, using `splat_labels.npy`. Across 440 objects that hides 21% fewer other splats than whole boxes, and still 99.8% of its own. Objects made in the viewer still use their whole box.\n- Walls and floor can't be picked or hovered in any BIM look.\n- Isolating in BIM shows only that object's label. Hidden types lose their labels too.\n- Frames are coloured by type, using BIM's groups, with a legend under More. The faulty device stays red.\n\n**Tested:**\n- 290+ tests with the Excel pack, lint clean.\n- On the ThinkPad's real GPU: 12 of 12 viewer checks, and 28 of 28 combine, delete, duplicate and back checks.\n- 66 of 66 route checks.\n\n**Not tested:** Gemma's \"In plain words\" on the new answers, a tablet, the 5090. The Val test was read by eye, not scored.\n\n**Decision needed:** Benjamin turned adaptive resolution off because of flicker. Turning is 16 frames a second by default, and 32 with `?adaptive=1`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\ngh pr create --base main --head viktor/polish --title \"Make Val talk like a person, and fix refused moves, Delete and BIM picks\" --body-file \"$S/pr8.md\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-80; sleep 8; timeout 100 gh pr checks viktor/polish --watch --interval 8 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-60; gh pr view viktor/polish --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus,number --jq '\"#\\(.number) \\(.mergeable) \\(.mergeStateStatus)\"'","description":"Run final checks, commit, push and open the pull request","timeout":280000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"14d175c6-f700-4365-9f76-330ed4990abd","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgp2kRg9sQ9ThRF9LyU26","requestRef":"82fecf35-7eb1-4f49-938e-9eae8044de77","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"265dd207-4009-47db-845c-2fe357c67864","timestamp":"2026-11-07T18:21:14.219Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/polish","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
