{"parentUuid":"9230b133-0ed2-457e-ac15-72a30c0f1a04","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgp2zkoyjm61c34678erD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1131,"cache_read_input_tokens":852631,"output_tokens":2523,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":889},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1131,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2523,"cache_read_input_tokens":852631,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1131},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":17196,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"c6981dc2-18ff-494c-95a6-c84e85a27b36","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgp2zkTePPy8yygLVig2o","requestRef":"95d13017-a56d-4c33-afa9-c5759a1965c1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"6bbdd793-11ce-49b2-9689-d5055e67d2c8","timestamp":"2026-11-07T18:24:16.634Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/polish","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"6bbdd793-11ce-49b2-9689-d5055e67d2c8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgp2zkoyjm61c34678erD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**All the fixes are done and ready as [#38](https://github.com/Sairanyx/Newbies/pull/38), but not merged yet: say \"merge\" and I will.** CI passes, and Benjamin's fixes were already on main, so #38 is built on them.\n\n## What's fixed\n- **Refused moves:** they now say why and record nothing. The misleading \"N objects moved\" count is gone.\n- **Delete:** it hides small boxes around the object's own splats, so 21% fewer neighbouring splats go overall, while 99.8% of the object's own still go. That total is a modest gain, and objects made in the viewer still use their whole box.\n- **Floor and walls:** can't be clicked or hovered in any BIM look.\n- **Isolate:** shows only that object's label, as in your screenshot.\n- **Frame colours:** they match BIM's groups: pumps amber, tanks green, valves purple, pipes blue, cables yellow, cabinets teal, chairs and shelves pink, everything else grey, and the fault red. The legend is under **More**.\n\n## Val\nI read about 90 prompts by eye, and it found real failures, now fixed:\n- **Not refused:** \"Shut it down\" and \"Can I restart it?\".\n- **Wrongly refused:** \"What does drain mean?\".\n- **Wrong target:** \"Take me to the kitchen\" routed to the last device, and \"Is the valve open?\" answered about a pump.\n\nIt also talks more like a person now:\n\n| | Answer |\n|---|---|\n| **Before** | Asset P-005 (ASSET-017) condition is 'attention_required' with health score 44/100... |\n| **Now** | P-005 needs attention. Its health is 44 out of 100, and the records point to efficiency loss / fouling-like signature. I'd start with this check: inspect hydraulic path. Follow the site's safety rules before touching anything. |\n\nAsking about vibration on P-005 now gets \"I don't have vibration readings\", plus what is measured. \"Is it safe?\" gets \"I can't tell you that it's safe\". Voice starts off, as Eduard's checklist asked.\n\n**Limit:** Val still works from code rules, not free conversation, so a phrasing I didn't test can still miss. Gemma's \"In plain words\" line hasn't been retested on the new answers.\n\n## Your questions\n**Adding new objects:** **Add object** only draws a box around splats already in the scan, so an object that was never scanned has no splats at all. Adding one properly would mean filming it, training splats on the 5090, lining them up with the room, merging them in, then segmenting and labelling. None of that exists, and I'd guess days of work, not hours. I'd pitch it as future work; **Duplicate** covers \"another one of these\" for now.\n\n**Voice mode:** it's light. Measured on this ThinkPad's CPU with one clean 11-second sample:\n\n| Model | Download | Time for 11 s of speech | RAM |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `tiny.en` | 75 MB | 0.6 s | 0.28 GB |\n| `base.en` | 141 MB | 0.9 s | 0.35 GB |\n| `small.en` | 464 MB | 2.2 s | 0.64 GB |\n\nI'd use `base.en`. Spoken replies can use the browser's built-in voice, which adds nothing to install. The catches are that a tablet's microphone needs HTTPS, and accuracy in a noisy plant is untested. The checklist already says this is the first thing to cut, so I'd only build it after the video is done.\n\n**Demo site:** visitors wouldn't overload it the way you fear, because each visitor's own GPU draws the room. The real problems are:\n- **GitHub Pages can't run it:** Pages can't run our API or model, and the repo is private.\n- **Shared state:** the backend keeps one copy of the room, so one visitor's moves and undos would hit everyone.\n- **Your laptop:** it would have to stay on and exposed, and the model answers one question at a time.\n- **Valmet's data:** publishing their scan needs their permission.\n\n**My suggestion:** skip the live URL, since it's optional. Submit the video and run it live for judges on site. If you really want a link, the safest version is a read-only page with the 22 MB light scene and canned answers, only with Valmet's OK. I'd guess about half a day.\n\n## Decision for you\n**Adaptive resolution:** Benjamin turned it off because it caused flicker, so the 31 frames/s I reported no longer applies by default. Turning is now 16 frames/s, or 32 with `?adaptive=1`. Hover did improve: 50 frames/s while moving the mouse, up from 19. Do you want me to fix the flicker and turn it back on? I'd say yes, as 16 will look rough in the video.\n\nWith the deadline at 10:00 tomorrow, the 5090 rehearsal, the video and asking Valmet about P-005 matter more than any further polish."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1131,"cache_read_input_tokens":852631,"output_tokens":2523,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":889},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1131,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2523,"cache_read_input_tokens":852631,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1131},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c6981dc2-18ff-494c-95a6-c84e85a27b36","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgp2zkTePPy8yygLVig2o","requestRef":"95d13017-a56d-4c33-afa9-c5759a1965c1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e9b8cf3-3b8c-452a-a26c-bfb54e4000a9","timestamp":"2026-11-07T18:24:25.166Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/w